// Status: experimental | Level: medium
// Author: Sri Charan
// Date: 2026-07-28 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: persistence, T1098.004
// Description: Detects the creation or modification of the 'authorized_keys' file on Linux systems. Attackers
//   often modify this file to maintain persistence by adding their own public key to a user's
//   authorized_keys file.
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate administration activities (e.g. ssh-copy-id)
//   - Configuration management tools (Ansible, Chef, Puppet) managing SSH keys
// References:
//   - https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1098/004/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/f57bdbd709668e28baec600abd0f0ba85a1fbadf/rules/linux/file_event/file_event_lnx_ssh_authorized_keys_modification.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceFileEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "/.ssh/authorized_keys" and (not(InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "/sshd"))
